  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Hydroboration&ndash;oxidation is an anti-Markovnikov reaction, with the hydroxyl group attaching to the less-substituted carbon.&nbsp;In an oxymercuration&ndash;demercuration reaction, an alkene is treated with mercury(II) acetate, and the product is treated with sodium borohydride. The net result is a Markovnikov addition product in which the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>OH</mi></math> group bonds to the more substituted carbon atom of the alkene.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0070_4b6d2e895016.png\" style=\"width: 399px; height: 180px;\" /></p>"
  }
